abstract: "For alpha > -1, every even-size Hankel determinant of the complex weight (1-t^2)^alpha e^{ixt} on [-1,1] is strictly positive for every real frequency x, extending the alpha = 0 theorem of Celsus, Deano, Huybrechs and Iserles (2022). So the even-degree orthogonal polynomials used in complex Gaussian quadrature for oscillatory integrals always exist; odd-size determinants have infinitely many real zeros. Every complex zero of every determinant is simple. The same large-frequency expansion proves the formal degree conjectures of Milovanovic, Cvetkovic and Marjanovic (2008) and gives complete proofs of Conjectures 2.5 and 2.7 of Lyu and Zhou (2026). A ResearchGate preprint of J. M. Ashfaque (24 July 2026) earlier claimed those recurrence formulas; its Proposition 3.1 fails as printed. Existence only; not node distinctness or conditioning. Unrefereed candidate; internal AI-assisted review only. Text CC0-1.0; code MIT."
